From 7a648d598cb8e8c62af3f0e020a25820a3f3a9a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Gu <ustc.gu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Feb 2026 23:14:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: pinconf-generic: Fix memory leak in
 pinconf_generic_parse_dt_config()

In pinconf_generic_parse_dt_config(), if parse_dt_cfg() fails, it returns
directly. This bypasses the cleanup logic and results in a memory leak of
the cfg buffer.

Fix this by jumping to the out label on failure, ensuring kfree(cfg) is
called before returning.

Fixes: 90a18c512884 ("pinctrl: pinconf-generic: Handle string values for generic properties")
Signed-off-by: Felix Gu <ustc.gu@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Antonio Borneo <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c b/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
index 94b1d057197c..2b030bd0e6ad 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c
@@ -351,13 +351,13 @@ int pinconf_generic_parse_dt_config(struct device_node *np,

 	ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, dt_params, ARRAY_SIZE(dt_params), cfg, &ncfg);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto out;
 	if (pctldev && pctldev->desc->num_custom_params &&
 		pctldev->desc->custom_params) {
 		ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, pctldev->desc->custom_params,
 				   pctldev->desc->num_custom_params, cfg, &ncfg);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto out;
 	}

 	/* no configs found at all */
-- 
2.34.1

## Summary of Modifications

### File modified: `drivers/pinctrl/pinconf-generic.c`

The patch fixes a memory leak in the function `pinconf_generic_parse_dt_config()`. In two error paths, when `parse_dt_cfg()` fails, the function previously returned `ret` directly, bypassing the cleanup logic that frees the `cfg` buffer. The fix replaces these early returns with `goto out;`, so that execution jumps to the existing `out` label (which calls `kfree(cfg)`) before returning.

**Original code (before fix):**
```c
ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, dt_params, ARRAY_SIZE(dt_params), cfg, &ncfg);
if (ret)
    return ret;
...
ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, pctldev->desc->custom_params,
                   pctldev->desc->num_custom_params, cfg, &ncfg);
if (ret)
    return ret;
```

**Fixed code (after patch):**
```c
ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, dt_params, ARRAY_SIZE(dt_params), cfg, &ncfg);
if (ret)
    goto out;
...
ret = parse_dt_cfg(np, pctldev->desc->custom_params,
                   pctldev->desc->num_custom_params, cfg, &ncfg);
if (ret)
    goto out;
```

### Relationship between modifications

The two changes are identical in nature—both are error-handling path corrections. They ensure that upon failure of either `parse_dt_cfg()` call, the function does not exit prematurely but instead proceeds to the common cleanup section at the `out` label, where the dynamically allocated `cfg` buffer is freed. This prevents a memory leak that would occur if the function returned without freeing `cfg` when an error was encountered before the cleanup point. The relationship is that both fixes address the same root cause (missing cleanup on error) in two separate but similar `parse_dt_cfg()` invocations within the same function.

